# Firebase MCP Access

The Firebase MCP server (`plugin-firebase-firebase`) is enabled for this project.  
Active project: **solara-stiven-dev** (alias: `default`).  
Signed-in account: `johnstiven40@gmail.com`. The previous project `hackathon-cursor` is not accessible from this account.

## How to use it

Always call `firebase_get_environment` first to confirm auth status and active project before using any other tool.

If `Authenticated User` is `<NONE>`, call `firebase_login` so the user can authenticate before proceeding.

## Available tools

| Tool | What it does |
|------|-------------|
| `firebase_get_environment` | Get active project, auth user, firebase.json |
| `firebase_login` / `firebase_logout` | Authenticate with Firebase |
| `firebase_list_projects` | List all Firebase projects |
| `firebase_get_project` | Get details for a specific project |
| `firebase_list_apps` / `firebase_create_app` | Manage web/Android/iOS apps |
| `firebase_get_sdk_config` | Get SDK config for an app |
| `firebase_get_security_rules` | Read Firestore / RTDB / Storage rules (type: `firestore` \| `rtdb` \| `storage`) |
| `firebase_init` | Initialize Firebase features (Firestore, Hosting, Auth…) |
| `functions_list_functions` | List deployed Cloud Functions |
| `functions_get_logs` | Fetch Cloud Function logs |
| `developerknowledge_answer_query` | Answer questions using official Firebase docs |

## Firestore specifics

- To read current security rules: call `firebase_get_security_rules` with `type: "firestore"`.
- Firestore and Google Sign-In are configured in `firebase.json`. The web SDK config lives in `lib/firebase.ts`.
- The client reads Firestore without sesión de Firebase en el rol de planta. Las reglas permiten lectura pública y solo actualizan alarmas si hay un usuario autenticado.
